      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "In 1893, South Bend citizens sailed to Oysterville, seized county books, and secured the county seat after a heated dispute.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        10
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://southbend-wa.gov/city/history-of-south-bend/",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The railroad reached South Bend in 1893, but never extended to Yakima, curbing hopes of becoming a major eastern Washington port.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        10
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://southbend-wa.gov/city/history-of-south-bend/",
      "category": "transport",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The Pacific County Courthouse, listed on the National Register of Historic Places, stands as a landmark of the town’s civic history.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
